(# Technical Design Document) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(**GitHub:** https://github.com/ashucfx/isocode-cardealership) Tj T*
(**Live application:** Not deployed; local run instructions are in `deployment.md`.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Problem and scope) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Brand X needs a premium customer journey that converts browsing into a test-drive lead and gives) Tj T*
(consultants an actionable inbox. This build covers inventory, transparent Lucknow pricing,) Tj T*
(test-drive booking, lead assignment, consultant assistance, and admin pricing control. Payments,) Tj T*
(DMS, WhatsApp, service booking, and analytics are future scope.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Assumptions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Lucknow is the initial city and has two fictional showrooms.) Tj T*
(- Admin is the authorized used-car pricing role.) Tj T*
(- A local JSON repository is used for zero-dependency evaluation; the route and domain boundaries) Tj T*
(are designed for PostgreSQL/Prisma replacement. This is an explicit take-home trade-off, not a) Tj T*
(production database recommendation.) Tj T*
(- AI output is assistance only and must be reviewed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Architecture) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Node server exposes REST-like JSON routes and serves a responsive static client. Domain) Tj T*
(operations \(price calculation, booking conflict checks, assignment and authorization\) execute) Tj T*
(server-side. The client renders API data and never owns authoritative state.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Business rules) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(`onRoad = exShowroom + roadTax + insurance + accessories`. Only active, non-expired city records) Tj T*
(participate. Test-drive uniqueness is enforced by showroom/date/slot. A new lead is assigned to a) Tj T*
(consultant at the selected showroom; an unassigned lead is never silently presented as owned.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Security and privacy) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Role checks run on every protected endpoint. Session cookies are HttpOnly and SameSite. Booking) Tj T*
(requires explicit consent, and registration numbers are masked before leaving the server. Production) Tj T*
(requires hashed passwords, HTTPS, rate limiting, CSRF protection and a managed secret store.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## AI) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The server constructs prompts from the lead and vehicle records only. In a deployed environment,) Tj T*
(`AI_PROVIDER_URL` and `AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY` connect this boundary to the configured server-side LLM) Tj T*
(provider; keys never reach the browser. Summary and reply are separate, labelled actions; drafts are) Tj T*
(editable and never sent automatically. The local demo uses a deterministic development adapter so) Tj T*
(reviewers can exercise the complete UI without a third-party key. In production, provider output) Tj T*
(must be schema-validated and rejected on malformed or unsupported content. No AI output affects) Tj T*
(price, inventory or booking availability.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
